  {
   "id": "6MmRjmSiCQAJ",
   "from": "Vladimir Mikryukov",
   "author": "f6b42639a030648b",
   "date": "2018-04-09T10:21:13Z",
   "subject": "Standard errors of the response variable in the model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello!<br>I would like to incorporate the standard errors for the response variable into the analysis.<br>Brms is wonderful package and, to my knowledge, it is the only one capable of doing so.<br><br>In general, I would like to fit the following model: `<b>S ~ A + B</b>`<br>where S is the species diversity estimate, and A &amp; B are experimental factors.<br><br>The true diversity is unknown (because of the unseen species), however we can estimate some uncertainty associated with it.<br>So I can try to use the `<b>S | se(<a href=\"http://S.SE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://S.SE&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451247080000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1v-XS7NZES5yRoVUjELREB\">S.SE</a>) ~ A + B</b>` model.<br><br>Standard error of S depends on the number of sampled individuals <br>(the more individuals we sample, the more we should know about the diversity).<br>In principal, I can try to use `<b>S | se(<a href=\"http://S.SE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://S.SE&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451247080000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1v-XS7NZES5yRoVUjELREB\">S.SE</a>, sigma = TRUE) ~ A + B, sigma ~ NumSamples</b>`<br><br>Is it a proper way of the analysis or there is something I&#39;m missing?<br><br><br>Here are some dummy data illustrating the structure of my dataset:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">datt </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  S </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mean </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sd </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mean </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">15</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sd </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#606\">NumSamples</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">200</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> size </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">40</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  A </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;A&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;a&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> each </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> B </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;B&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>datt$S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">SE </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">datt$NumSamples </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>modd </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> brm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    bf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> se</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">SE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> A </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">NumSamples</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> datt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> family </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gaussian</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    prior </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prior</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">student_t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">class</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> b</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>I really appreciate any help or advice you can provide.<br>With best regards,<br>Vladimir<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "6ilUt8qLCQAJ",
   "from": "Paul Buerkner",
   "author": "6e3dd74b422c061b",
   "date": "2018-04-10T17:36:56Z",
   "subject": "Re: [brms-users] Standard errors of the response variable in the model",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>The problem I see with this approach is that the standard error is in your example proportional to 1/n, while it is usually proportional to 1/sqrt(n).<br><br></div>Since the main purpose of this seems to be a weighting of each observation(?), have you considered using the weights() instead of the se() argument?<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">2018-04-09 12:21 GMT+02:00 Vladimir Mikryukov <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">vmikr...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span>:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello!<br>I would like to incorporate the standard errors for the response variable into the analysis.<br>Brms is wonderful package and, to my knowledge, it is the only one capable of doing so.<br><br>In general, I would like to fit the following model: `<b>S ~ A + B</b>`<br>where S is the species diversity estimate, and A &amp; B are experimental factors.<br><br>The true diversity is unknown (because of the unseen species), however we can estimate some uncertainty associated with it.<br>So I can try to use the `<b>S | se(<a href=\"http://S.SE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://S.SE&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451247086000&amp;usg=AOvVaw39nZjSO4YPemoGUHJLrM3E\">S.SE</a>) ~ A + B</b>` model.<br><br>Standard error of S depends on the number of sampled individuals <br>(the more individuals we sample, the more we should know about the diversity).<br>In principal, I can try to use `<b>S | se(<a href=\"http://S.SE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://S.SE&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451247087000&amp;usg=AOvVaw253P-ALrqoXgIJ2Nj1oxHH\">S.SE</a>, sigma = TRUE) ~ A + B, sigma ~ NumSamples</b>`<br><br>Is it a proper way of the analysis or there is something I&#39;m missing?<br><br><br>Here are some dummy data illustrating the structure of my dataset:<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">datt </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  S </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mean </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sd </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rnorm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mean </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">15</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sd </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#606\">NumSamples</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">200</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> size </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">40</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  A </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;A&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;a&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> each </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> B </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> rep</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;B&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;b&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>datt$S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">SE </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> round</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">/</span><span style=\"color:#000\">datt$NumSamples </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>modd </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> brm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    bf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S </span><span style=\"color:#660\">|</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> se</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">S</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">SE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> A </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> B</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma </span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">NumSamples</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> datt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> family </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gaussian</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    prior </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prior</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">student_t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">class</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> b</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>I really appreciate any help or advice you can provide.<br>With best regards,<br>Vladimir<span><font color=\"#888888\"><br></font></span></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><span><font color=\"#888888\">\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;brms-users&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">brms-users+unsubscribe@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">brms-...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/brms-users/876903a9-fe7c-4fb9-8e45-56617ba2f7d2%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/brms-users/876903a9-fe7c-4fb9-8e45-56617ba2f7d2%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451247087000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0DuMr9oleHRNPVqAmAsW03\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/brms-users/876903a9-fe7c-4fb9-8e45-56617ba2f7d2%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792451247087000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3K8lGWLrBhwEI-WcCwLORM\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</font></span></blockquote></div><br></div>\r\n"
